Subject: [PATCH] auth: drive the Entra ID + Duo Universal Prompt login chain

Some institutions' identity providers no longer serve the older single-sign-on
form this module waits for. They delegate to Microsoft Entra ID, which presents
an email step, then a password step, then a second-factor prompt (commonly Duo's
Universal Prompt), then a "Stay signed in?" page. The published build waits for a
selector that never appears on that chain, so automated login hangs on a page
that is fully rendered and fully ignored. Manual login works; automated login
never completes; nothing says why.

This drives the chain that is actually there, keeps the older selectors as a
fallback so schools still on the previous flow are unaffected, and throws
DISTINGUISHABLE errors so a caller can tell "the password was rejected" apart
from "the second factor was never approved". Those are opposite problems with
opposite fixes, and collapsing them into one generic failure is what makes an
auth break take an afternoon to diagnose instead of a minute.

It also softens two networkidle waits: an LMS home page that keeps polling
connections open never goes idle, so the wait always burns its full timeout on a
page that has been usable for seconds.

---------------------------------------------------------------------------
 HOW TO APPLY THIS — READ BEFORE YOU RUN ANYTHING
---------------------------------------------------------------------------

 1. YOU PROBABLY DO NOT NEED IT. Try the ordinary path first:
        npx -y brightspace-mcp-server@latest auth
    Only if that HANGS on your school's login page does this file apply to you.
    See docs/connectors/brightspace.md, which walks the whole decision.

 2. PREFER INSTALLING FROM UPSTREAM `main`. These fixes may already be merged
    there even when they are not on npm yet, and an upstream install needs no
    patching and no local build. That option is written up in NOTICE.md.

 3. THE FILE PATH BELOW IS A PLACEHOLDER. Upstream names this module after the
    university it was originally written for, and that name is not stable across
    versions. Find the real one:
        ls node_modules/brightspace-mcp-server/build/auth/
    then edit the two `---` / `+++` lines below to match before applying.

 4. THIS IS A REFERENCE PATCH, NOT A BYTE-EXACT DIFF. The hunk line numbers are
    approximate and the surrounding context will have drifted. Apply it with
    fuzz, or read it and make the same changes by hand:
        patch -p1 --fuzz=5 < entra-duo-sso.patch
    If a hunk is rejected, the `+` side below is complete enough to paste in.

 5. NEVER PATCH A PACKAGE MANAGER'S CACHE. Writing into node_modules inside an
    npx or npm cache is invisible, survives nothing, and produces a machine
    whose behaviour cannot be reproduced from its configuration. Take a real
    checkout, patch that, build it, and point .mcp.json at your build.

 6. THE SAML ENTITY ID IS YOUR SCHOOL'S, NOT A CONSTANT. The navigation below
    reads it from the environment so the same build works anywhere:
        LMS_SAML_ENTITY_ID=https://idp.example.edu/idp/shibboleth
    Find yours by opening your LMS login page and reading the link behind your
    institution's button in the campus selector.

